course: dictionary
lesson: 13203
title: Words about how things work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word functionally comes from function, which means the job something does. So when you say something works functionally, you are talking about what it does, not how it looks.
explain: «The red mug and the blue cup are functionally the same, because both hold tea.» The clue is the word same. Their jobs are the same, even though their colours are different.
explain: Grown-ups also use functionally to mean "for practical purposes" or "in effect". «The broken lamp is functionally useless» means it cannot do its job, even if it still looks nice on the shelf.
fact: Functionally is an adverb. It tells you how something works or does its job.
fact: «Functionally» means in a way that is about how something works, not how it looks.
fact: «Functionally» can also mean for practical purposes, or in effect.
fact: Phrases you may meet are functionally the same, functionally equivalent and functionally useless.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in "in what it does": «functionally the same» becomes "the same in what they do".
exercise: «The two bags are functionally the same, even though one is red and one is blue.» What does functionally mean here? | In colour | In a loud way | In size only | *In what they do, not how they look
exercise: In design and technology, Sam says, «The old phone is functionally fine.» What does Sam mean? | The phone is very heavy | The phone looks brand new | *The phone still does its job well | The phone is lost
exercise: «The torch has no battery, so it is functionally useless.» What does functionally useless mean? | It is very pretty | It is cheap to buy | It was made in a factory | *It cannot do its job, in effect
test: «Two calculators give the same answers, so they are functionally equivalent.» What does functionally equivalent mean? | They were bought on the same day | They look exactly alike | They cost the same money | *They work the same way and do the same job
test: «Ella says the rusty bike is functionally useless.» What is Ella saying? | The bike has a new bell | The bike is very fast | *The bike cannot do its job | The bike is a present for a friend
exam: What is the best swap for functionally in «The mug and the cup are functionally the same»? | in a hurry | in colour | *in what they do | loudly
